<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  PLACEHOLDER ORIGIN — not yet valid for production.

  Every <loc> below uses REPLACE-WITH-CANONICAL-ORIGIN.invalid because the canonical domain
  does not exist yet (the Netlify site is created in Phase 5, which is paused). `.invalid` is
  reserved by RFC 2606 and can never resolve, so submitting this as-is fails visibly rather
  than quietly advertising the wrong host. Replace the origin here and in robots.txt before
  the first production deploy.

  Scope: static public routes only. Project detail pages (/projects/:id) are deliberately
  absent — their URLs are UUIDs known only at runtime, and this is a build-time artifact in
  `frontend/public/`, which Netlify copies verbatim. Listing them needs either a build-time
  API call or a generation step, and the 2026-08-10 SEO ADR in docs/DECISIONS.md defers that
  alongside prerendering, for the same reason: it would make the Netlify build depend on the
  VPS backend, which the committed API client exists to avoid.

  Admin routes are omitted on purpose; robots.txt disallows them.

  No <lastmod>: a hardcoded date would be wrong the moment anything changes, and there is no
  build step here to generate a real one. An absent lastmod is honest; a stale one is a lie
  crawlers act on.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url>
    <loc>https://REPLACE-WITH-CANONICAL-ORIGIN.invalid/</loc>
    <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>
    <priority>1.0</priority>
  </url>
  <url>
    <loc>https://REPLACE-WITH-CANONICAL-ORIGIN.invalid/contact</loc>
    <changefreq>yearly</changefreq>
    <priority>0.5</priority>
  </url>
</urlset>
